<urn:atm:triage:finding/RBQA-AI3152TOOLING-F003>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "RBQA-AI3152TOOLING-F003" ;
  triage:title "No mechanical guard couples daemon-building recipes to the signing hook" ;
  triage:description "No lint prevents a future just recipe from building target/{debug,release}/atm-daemon while skipping sign_daemon_dev.py. Same repeated-leak-pattern class already covered for other conventions by .just/lint_boundaries.py / .just/lint_manifests.py, but signing-hook coupling has no equivalent check. Recommendation: add a lint (e.g. .just/lint_daemon_signing_coupling.py) that greps Justfile for every recipe invoking `cargo build ... atm-daemon` and asserts it also invokes sign_daemon_dev.py or composes through the shared build recipe." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "lint_gap" ;
  triage:severity "minor" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "workspace" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-08-03T18:45:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AI3152-CROSSHOST ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-08-03T18:35:45Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/RBQA-AI3152TOOLING-F003/RBQA-AI3152TOOLING-F003-001> ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "2" ;
  triage:progressNote "QA-2 (865b3308): a lint (.just/lint_daemon_signing_coupling.py) was added and wired into run_lint.py, but req-qa/arch-qa/ruthless-boundary-qa independently confirmed two real detection gaps that keep this open: (1) DAEMON_BUILD_RE requires the literal substring 'atm-daemon' on the same line as 'cargo build', so it never classifies the primary build: recipe's 'cargo build --workspace' (Justfile:134, no literal atm-daemon token) as a daemon-build line -- if the hook were dropped from build: the lint would report zero violations; (2) RECIPE_HEADER_RE cannot match Just's dependency-header syntax ('name: dep1 dep2', present at Justfile:7 and :206), so recipe_blocks() silently drops any daemon-build recipe written with that idiom. Neither gap is covered by the lint's own 5-test suite. Remains open pending a fix round." .

